course: dictionary
lesson: 8346
title: Room: a place or some space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Room has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «You smell cookies baking from the other room» means a part of a building with walls, a floor and a ceiling. Try swapping in place: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Room can also mean free space. «When passing a horse and rider, give lots of room» means leave plenty of space around them. The clues are passing and give lots of, so the meaning is space, not a building.
explain: Room can even mean a chance. «Room for improvement» means there is still space to get better. Look at the words next to room, such as living room, make room or no room, and they will show you which meaning the writer chose.
fact: A room is a part of a building with walls, a floor and a ceiling, like a kitchen or a bedroom.
fact: Room can also mean free space for someone or something, as in «give lots of room».
fact: «Room for» can mean a chance, as in «room for improvement».
fact: In «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room», room is the place where Chloe is looked after.
fact: Room can be a verb, but it is rare. It means to share a room with someone.
exercise: «You smell cookies baking from the other room.» What is a room here? | *A part of a building with walls, a floor and a ceiling | A kind of cookie | Free space for a horse to walk in | A chance to get better
exercise: «When passing a horse and rider, give lots of room.» What does room mean here? | A bedroom with a bed | A loud noise | A small cake | *Free space
exercise: What does «room for improvement» mean? | *A chance to get better | A big empty building | A place to keep horses | Free space in a box
test: «In a hospital or doctor's waiting room you speak quietly.» What kind of room is this? | A horse's stable | A chance to improve | Free space to walk around | *A place inside a building with walls and a floor
test: Jayden says, «There is no room for one more.» What does room mean? | A short rest | *Free space | A part of a building for sleeping | A kitchen with a table
exam: Which sentence uses room to mean a part of a building? | *«Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room» | «Make room for the wheelchair» | «Give lots of room to the horse» | «There is room for improvement»
